      "id": 1,
      "text": "Eight Mile Plains got its name early in settlement, referring to the flat land and its eight‑mile distance to One Mile Swamp.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Mile_Plains%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Eight Mile Plains busway station, part of the South‑East Busway, links the suburb to Brisbane’s public transport network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Mile_Plains%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bulimba Creek marks the northern and western edge of Eight Mile Plains, while the Gateway Motorway bounds it to the northeast and the Pacific Motorway to the southeast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Mile_Plains%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1864 the Eight Mile Plains Agricultural Reserve expanded by 5,500 acres, eventually encompassing what are now Sunnybank, Sunnybank Hills, Runcorn, Kuraby, and parts of Coopers Plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Mile_Plains%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hughesville, a beautiful 1892–93 house on Millers Road, is listed as a heritage site in Eight Mile Plains.",
